== 8.8 Chapter 8 Practice Drill — 30 Questions

30 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 33 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [Anaerobic respiration in human muscle produces],
  [lactic acid],
  [alcohol and carbon dioxide],
  [carbon dioxide and water],
  [glucose and oxygen]
)

#mcq(2, [Gas exchange in the lungs takes place in the],
  [trachea],
  [bronchi],
  [alveoli],
  [pleura]
)

#mcq(3, [During inspiration the diaphragm],
  [does not move],
  [relaxes and becomes domed],
  [contracts and flattens],
  [contracts and becomes domed]
)

#mcq(4, [Which statement about plants is correct?],
  [They do not respire],
  [They respire only at night],
  [They respire only in the dark],
  [They photosynthesise and respire in daylight]
)

#mcq(5, [The products of aerobic respiration are],
  [glucose and oxygen],
  [lactic acid and water],
  [carbon dioxide and water],
  [alcohol and carbon dioxide]
)

#mcq(6, [Anaerobic respiration in yeast produces],
  [glucose],
  [alcohol and carbon dioxide],
  [lactic acid],
  [carbon dioxide and water]
)

#mcq(7, [The energy released by respiration is used for all of the following except],
  [active transport],
  [absorbing light],
  [building proteins],
  [muscle contraction]
)

#mcq(8, [The alveolus wall is one cell thick in order to],
  [trap dust],
  [provide a short diffusion distance],
  [store air],
  [give strength]
)

#mcq(9, [The presence of carbon dioxide can be shown using],
  [limewater],
  [hydrogencarbonate indicator only],
  [iodine solution],
  [Benedict's solution]
)

#mcq(10, [Which factor keeps the concentration gradient at the alveolus steep?],
  [A thick wall],
  [A dry surface],
  [A small surface area],
  [A rich blood supply]
)

#mcq(11, [Anaerobic respiration releases less energy than aerobic respiration because],
  [glucose is only partly broken down],
  [oxygen is present],
  [glucose is not used],
  [no enzymes are involved]
)

#mcq(12, [Oxygen debt refers to],
  [the oxygen stored in the lungs],
  [the extra oxygen needed to break down accumulated lactic acid],
  [the oxygen carried by haemoglobin],
  [the oxygen used in photosynthesis]
)

#mcq(13, [Exhaled air differs from inhaled air in having],
  [less oxygen, more carbon dioxide and more water vapour],
  [more nitrogen],
  [more oxygen and less carbon dioxide],
  [no water vapour]
)

#mcq(14, [The trachea is prevented from collapsing by],
  [cartilage rings],
  [mucus],
  [bone],
  [muscle]
)

#mcq(15, [Which of these is an example of breathing?],
  [Glucose being broken down in a cell],
  [Air moving into the lungs],
  [Carbon dioxide being produced in muscle],
  [Oxygen diffusing into the blood]
)

#mcq(16, [The energy released by respiration is used to make],
  [chlorophyll],
  [starch only],
  [cellulose only],
  [ATP]
)

#mcq(17, [During expiration],
  [thoracic volume increases],
  [the diaphragm relaxes and becomes domed],
  [the ribs move up and out],
  [pressure in the thorax falls]
)

#mcq(18, [Which statement about the lungs is correct?],
  [They are solid and cannot expand],
  [They contain muscles that pump air],
  [They are inflated by pressure changes in the thorax],
  [They fill with blood during inspiration]
)

#mcq(19, [Which of these would increase the rate of breathing?],
  [Sleeping],
  [Sitting quietly],
  [Resting],
  [Vigorous exercise]
)

#mcq(20, [The respiratory surface of a fish is the],
  [gill filament],
  [skin],
  [alveolus],
  [trachea]
)

#mcq(21, [A respiratory surface must be all of the following except],
  [thin],
  [moist],
  [well supplied with blood],
  [dry]
)

#mcq(22, [Muscle fatigue after strenuous exercise is caused mainly by],
  [accumulation of lactic acid],
  [excess oxygen],
  [a lack of glucose],
  [a lack of water]
)

#mcq(23, [The correct equation for aerobic respiration is],
  [glucose → alcohol + carbon dioxide],
  [glucose → lactic acid + oxygen],
  [carbon dioxide + water → glucose + oxygen],
  [glucose + oxygen → carbon dioxide + water]
)

#mcq(24, [Which organ removes carbon dioxide from the body?],
  [Lungs],
  [Kidney],
  [Skin],
  [Liver]
)

#mcq(25, [Smoking damages the lungs mainly by],
  [increasing the alveolar surface area],
  [increasing oxygen uptake],
  [destroying cilia and alveoli and reducing surface area],
  [thickening the blood]
)

#mcq(26, [A plant kept in the dark produces carbon dioxide because],
  [it is photosynthesising],
  [photosynthesis stops but respiration continues],
  [respiration stops],
  [it is dead]
)

#mcq(27, [The gas exchange surface of an insect is the],
  [skin],
  [alveolus],
  [tracheal system],
  [gill]
)

#mcq(28, [Which of these is *not* a product of respiration?],
  [Water],
  [Energy],
  [Carbon dioxide],
  [Chlorophyll]
)

#mcq(29, [The rate of breathing is controlled mainly by the concentration of],
  [nitrogen in the air],
  [oxygen in the blood],
  [carbon dioxide in the blood],
  [glucose in the blood]
)

#mcq(30, [Breathing faster and deeper than necessary after exercise is called],
  [vital capacity],
  [oxygen debt],
  [tidal volume],
  [residual volume]
)

